  "description": "VUVKII crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H220 N10 O50 Tb10,4(C2 H3 N1),8(C1 H1 Cl3). From the CIF bond table, Tb1P (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2P (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3P (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4P (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5P (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb9 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb10 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb1Q (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2Q (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3Q (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4Q (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5Q (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb16 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb17 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb18 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb19 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb20 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.803-3.839 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.49-114.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C176H240Cl24N14O50Tb10.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
